docs/research/agent-studio-landscape-2026-09-21.md:28:Mast suggests these design proposals, which are not implemented or adopted: use schema versions, validation, atomic state writes, a single writer or per-resource locking, and retention of the last known-good record after corruption; use append-only events and evidence with safe interrupted-tail recovery; bound disposable terminal output; rebuild fresh worker briefs from durable records; clear stale process IDs and reconcile in-flight work without falsely marking it done; separate UI layout from product knowledge; and send structured checked task messages instead of arbitrary shell injection. Test interrupted save/restart, duplicate events, and worker disappearance. Durable Bisellium roles, tasks, decisions, and evidence remain authoritative; Mast-style runtime state must not become semantic memory.
docs/research/agent-studio-landscape-2026-09-21.md:44:Keep boot bundles task-specific: authority, role, acceptance criteria, relevant decisions, and latest handoff first; summaries before source files; per-section token caps; and links to durable locations when material is omitted. Each handoff should capture decisions, changes, blockers, and next steps. Keep journals, transcripts, receipts, and completed history searchable outside the prompt, and refresh the bundle at task boundaries. The `context` command is a natural enforcement point for size, duplication, staleness, and omitted-link checks. Measure context overhead alongside errors and rework so smaller prompts do not hide information needed for correct work. `retro`, `tick`, and `context` can identify, revisit, and load validated remedies, but this remains a proposal rather than policy.
docs/research/agent-studio-landscape-2026-09-21.md:46:Standing documents should name their owner, authoritative sources, and review or retirement trigger. Owners may make factual corrections; goals, permissions, and policy changes require the appropriate decision. Consolidate duplicate guidance, archive historical material while preserving short dated snapshots, and update affected documents with implementation work. Change templates or structured records before regenerating `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and similar files. Checks should continue to cover links, instruction size, generated drift, review dates, and implementation changes that lack an affected-document link.
